var e=(e,t,n)=>({id:e,title:t,text:n}),t=(e,t)=>({label:`Zelda's Palace · ${t}`,href:`https://www.zeldaspalace.com/ocarinaoftime/soluce.php?p=${e}`}),n=(e,t)=>({label:`Thonky · ${t}`,href:`https://www.thonky.com/ocarina-of-time/${e}`}),r=(e,t)=>({label:`Zelda Dungeon · ${t}`,href:`https://www.zeldadungeon.net/ocarina-of-time-walkthrough/${e}/`}),i=`A complete main-story route for the original Nintendo 64 quest: every required dungeon, item and story connection, from Kokiri Forest to the final battle. Optional heart pieces, all 100 Gold Skulltulas and Master Quest are outside this route.`,a=[{slug:`deku-tree`,title:`Inside the Deku Tree`,subtitle:`The forest calls your name.`,description:`Find Link's first equipment, descend through the Deku Tree and defeat Queen Gohma in the original N64 quest.`,era:`Child Link`,region:`Kokiri Forest`,reward:`Fairy Slingshot · Kokiri's Emerald`,prerequisites:[`A new original-quest save`],steps:[e(`sword-shield`,`Equip a sword and shield`,`From Link's house, visit the fenced training area. Crawl through its small opening; follow the rolling-boulder maze to the chest with the Kokiri Sword. Collect 40 Rupees around the village and buy a Deku Shield in the shop. Equip both on the pause screen, then speak to Mido on the path to the Deku Tree.`),e(`slingshot`,`Climb to the slingshot`,`Enter the tree and climb the lobby ladder. Follow the walkway past the map chest. In the side room, face the Deku Scrub with your shield raised to reflect its nut, then speak to it. Cross the next room and open the large chest for the Fairy Slingshot. Shoot the ladder above the entrance if your return platform has fallen.`),e(`upper-floor`,`Reach the highest walkway`,`Back in the lobby, shoot the Skullwalltulas on the vines before climbing to the upper ring. Clear a hanging Skulltula by waiting for its vulnerable belly to face you. Cross the nearby compass room (only its chest is optional); use its switch to raise platforms and light its unlit torch with a Deku Stick to leave.`),e(`break-web`,`Break the floor web`,`Jump from the upper walkway toward the middle of the web far below. A properly centered landing tears it and drops you into the basement. Step on the basement switch to light the protected torch.`),e(`first-fire`,`Carry fire across the water`,`Light a Deku Stick at that torch. Use the shallow section of water to reach the web-covered doorway without submerging the flame, then touch the web with the stick. Deflect the next Scrub's nut and hear its clue. Shoot the eye above the next door.`),e(`water-switch`,`Pass beneath the spiked roller`,`Dive onto the underwater switch to lower the water temporarily. Ride the moving platform underneath the roller. On the far side, defeat the Skulltula, move the block under the ledge and climb to the exit.`),e(`return-ledge`,`Reach the upper basement ledge`,`Light both unlit torches in the following room. In the next chamber, burn the web leading to the small crawlspace and crawl through it. You emerge above the first basement room. Push its block off the ledge to create a return step.`),e(`second-web`,`Burn the second floor web`,`Get fire from the basement torch, climb back using the moved block and roll with the lit stick over the floor web. Drop into the lower room.`),e(`scrub-code`,`Use the Scrubs' order`,`Reflect nuts at the three Scrubs in this order: middle, right, left. Chase and speak to the final Scrub to unlock the boss chamber. Enter and look up to begin the encounter.`),e(`emerald`,`Return with the Emerald`,`After defeating Gohma, take the Heart Container and enter the blue light. Listen to the Deku Tree and receive Kokiri's Emerald. Leave the forest by its western exit; Saria gives you the Fairy Ocarina on the bridge.`)],boss:{name:`Queen Gohma`,strategy:[`Target her eye. When it turns red, a Slingshot shot stuns her; move in and strike with the sword.`,`If she climbs to the ceiling, shoot the red eye before she drops eggs. Otherwise, clear the hatched enemies and repeat the ground opening.`]},notes:[`On an N64 controller, Z targeting keeps combat readable. Button labels differ on modern controllers running the original game.`,`Save through the pause menu. The checklist here records your reading progress, not the game's save file.`],sources:[t(1,`Kokiri Forest`),t(2,`Inside the Deku Tree`),n(`inside-deku-tree`,`Deku Tree`),r(`inside-the-great-deku-tree`,`The first dungeon`)]},{slug:`princess-and-gorons`,title:`The princess & the Gorons`,subtitle:`A song can open a kingdom.`,description:`Meet Princess Zelda, learn the songs needed for the mountain and gain the Goron's Bracelet.`,era:`Child Link`,region:`Hyrule Castle · Lost Woods · Goron City`,reward:`Zelda's Letter · two songs · Goron's Bracelet`,prerequisites:[`Kokiri's Emerald`,`Fairy Ocarina`],steps:[e(`market`,`Travel to Hyrule Castle`,`Cross Hyrule Field toward the castle drawbridge. Enter during daylight; if it closes, wait for morning. Meet Malon in the market, then follow the northern exit toward the castle. Speak to her again by the vines to receive a Weird Egg; leaving and re-entering the castle approach makes her appear if necessary.`),e(`talon`,`Wake the sleeping rancher`,`Climb the vines beside Malon and get beyond the gate. Stay outside the guards' sight, cross the grassy slope and climb the rough wall near the castle. Swim along the moat to the corner with Talon. After the egg hatches at morning, use the chicken beside him.`),e(`courtyard`,`Reach Zelda's courtyard`,`Move the two milk crates into a stack at the moat edge. Climb them, jump to the opposite opening and crawl through during daytime. In the gardens, follow behind each guard patrol instead of crossing its view. Speak with Zelda, accept her request and take Zelda's Letter. Impa teaches Zelda's Lullaby as you leave.`),e(`saria`,`Visit Saria in the Sacred Forest Meadow`,`Return to Kokiri Forest and enter the Lost Woods through the high entrance. From its entrance, take right, left, right, left, straight, left, right. Defeat the Wolfos to open the gate. Work through the hedge maze, blocking Mad Scrub nuts, then climb the stairs. Speak to Saria to learn Saria's Song.`),e(`shield`,`Prepare for falling rocks and fire`,`A Hylian Shield protects against hazards that can burn the wooden shield. Buy one in the market, or visit Kakariko Graveyard at night and pull the flower-marked grave near the entrance for a free one. As a child, Link crouches under this shield rather than holding it forward.`),e(`gate`,`Open the Death Mountain gate`,`At Kakariko's northern gate, show Zelda's Letter to the guard using its assigned item button. Follow Death Mountain Trail uphill to the red flag, then turn toward Goron City.`),e(`darunia`,`Play for Darunia`,`Descend to Goron City's lowest level. Play Zelda's Lullaby on the mat in front of Darunia's door. Inside, speak to him and play Saria's Song. He gives the Goron's Bracelet, which lets child Link lift Bomb Flowers.`),e(`cavern`,`Unblock Dodongo's Cavern`,`Exit Goron City to the mountain trail. At the nearby fenced ledge, lift a Bomb Flower and throw it down toward the giant boulder sealing the cavern below. Reposition and repeat if it misses. Descend the path and enter the opened cavern.`)],notes:[`The Happy Mask trade is optional; the guard's request does not stop the main quest.`,`A bottle and Epona's Song are useful side trips at Lon Lon Ranch. The Adventure Journal has separate step-by-step entries for both.`],sources:[t(3,`Castle Town and Zelda`),t(4,`Lon Lon Ranch and Saria`),t(5,`Kakariko and the Gorons`)]},{slug:`dodongos-cavern`,title:`Dodongo's Cavern`,subtitle:`There is a heartbeat beneath the mountain.`,description:`Solve the Bomb Flower staircase, open the giant skull and prepare Link's magic for the rest of the journey.`,era:`Child Link`,region:`Death Mountain`,reward:`Bomb Bag · Goron's Ruby · magic · Din's Fire`,prerequisites:[`Goron's Bracelet`,`Slingshot`,`Deku Sticks`,`Hylian Shield recommended`],steps:[e(`lobby`,`Open the cavern`,`Use the entrance Bomb Flower to destroy the cracked wall. In the main lava chamber, ride the platforms to the lower east doorway and bomb its cracked wall. The map is behind a different cracked wall on the west side.`),e(`east-switch`,`Clear the eastern loop`,`Pass the Baby Dodongos; their bodies explode after defeat. Push an Armos statue onto the blue floor switch. Continue to the two Lizalfos and defeat both. In the next corridor, attack the larger Dodongos from behind, then light all three torches with a Deku Stick. Step on the switch at the end to open the west-side route.`),e(`stairs`,`Drop the enormous staircase`,`Cross the lobby to the newly opened west door. In the room lined with Bomb Flowers, place one flower in the empty gap between the two rows. The simultaneous chain explosion lowers the staircase. Climb it.`),e(`bridge`,`Cross above the lobby`,`In the upper room, move the statue blocking the ladder and climb to the switch. Avoid waking unnecessary Armos. Cross the bridge above the main chamber and continue into the blade-trap room.`),e(`timed-bomb`,`Break the high wall`,`Move the block under the ladder and use the raised area by the Bomb Flower. Hold a flower briefly before throwing it onto the cracked-wall ledge so it explodes there. Climb through the opening.`),e(`fire-platforms`,`Switch off the platform flames`,`Shoot the eye above the far door to cross the first flame platform. Defeat the next pair of Lizalfos. In the following room, shoot the first eye, jump to the middle platform and shoot the newly visible side eye to complete the crossing.`),e(`bomb-bag`,`Collect the Bomb Bag`,`Continue over the upper blade-trap room to the large chest. The Bomb Bag lets you carry and place your own bombs. Step on the nearby switch to extend the lobby elevator.`),e(`eyes`,`Light the skull's eyes`,`Stand on the bridge above the giant stone skull. Drop one bomb through each of the two openings so it detonates inside an eye socket. When both eyes glow, the mouth opens. Descend and enter it.`),e(`last-block`,`Unlock the last door`,`From the mouth room, take the right-hand passage around the block puzzle. Climb and move through the loop until you can push the block into the central hole, weighing down its switch. Enter the unlocked room and bomb its cracked floor.`),e(`ruby`,`Claim the second Spiritual Stone`,`Drop into King Dodongo's arena. After the battle, take the Heart Container and blue warp. Darunia gives you Goron's Ruby outside.`),e(`magic`,`Visit the mountain Great Fairy`,`Climb above the red flag, bombing the rocks in your way. Shelter under the Hylian Shield during the falling-rock bursts, then keep moving. Clear the Skullwalltulas and climb to the summit. Bomb the wall beside the owl; inside, play Zelda's Lullaby on the Triforce to receive magic and the charged spin attack.`),e(`dins-fire`,`Pick up Din's Fire now`,`Return to the Hyrule Castle approach as a child. Bomb the large rock at the dead-end near the entrance area, crawl into the fountain and play Zelda's Lullaby. Keep Din's Fire: it will open the Shadow Temple later. You can now head toward Zora's River.`)],boss:{name:`King Dodongo`,strategy:[`When he inhales with his mouth wide open, throw a bomb into it. Strike with the sword while he is stunned.`,`Move onto the narrow safe bank beside the lava while he rolls past. Avoid the lava itself, then repeat when he stops.`]},notes:[`Do not leave the magic visit until the Shadow Temple entrance; this route collects both magic and Din's Fire while child Link is already nearby.`],sources:[n(`dodongos-cavern`,`Cavern route`),t(6,`Dodongo's Cavern`),t(7,`Magic and Din's Fire`),r(`dodongos-cavern`,`Bomb Bag and King Dodongo`)]},{slug:`jabu-jabu`,title:`Inside Jabu-Jabu`,subtitle:`Carry a princess. Trust a boomerang.`,description:`Reach Zora's Fountain, rescue Ruto and free Jabu-Jabu from Barinade.`,era:`Child Link`,region:`Zora's Domain · Zora's Fountain`,reward:`Silver Scale · bottle · Boomerang · Zora's Sapphire`,prerequisites:[`Bomb Bag`,`Zelda's Lullaby`,`20 Rupees for the diving game`],steps:[e(`domain`,`Open the waterfall`,`Enter Zora's River from Hyrule Field and bomb the rocks blocking the path. Follow the banks uphill. At the waterfall, stand on the Triforce mark, play Zelda's Lullaby and jump through the opening.`),e(`letter`,`Find Ruto's letter`,`From King Zora's chamber, take the left passage to the diving game. Pay 20 Rupees, collect all the thrown rupees in time and return for the Silver Scale. Dive through the underwater tunnel to Lake Hylia. Retrieve the bottled letter on the lakebed near the exit, return through the tunnel and show it to King Zora.`),e(`feed`,`Enter the guardian`,`After the king moves, the letter's bottle becomes reusable. Catch a fish in Zora's Domain's shallow water. Follow the passage behind the king to the fountain and release the fish directly in front of Jabu-Jabu's mouth.`),e(`ruto`,`Catch up with Princess Ruto`,`Shoot the fleshy ceiling switch in the first room. Cross the elevator room without dropping below, then speak to Ruto in the room with floor holes. Follow her down, speak until she agrees to be carried, and pick her up.`),e(`carry`,`Carry her back upstairs`,`Take the side passage. Throw Ruto onto the far ledge before stepping on the floor switch that raises the water. Retrieve her, activate the ceiling switch beyond, then defeat or avoid the Octorok and ride the platform back to the upper level. Carry her across the hole room to the far doorway.`),e(`boomerang`,`Use her weight to reach the Boomerang`,`In the branching corridor, head right. Stand on the yellow switch while holding Ruto. Inside, defeat every Stinger; approach to make them rise, then hit them with the Slingshot or sword. Open the chest for the Boomerang.`),e(`tentacles`,`Remove the parasitic tentacles`,`At the opposite end of the branching corridor, leave Ruto on the blue switch and enter. Target the hanging red tentacle and stun its narrow middle with the Boomerang until it falls. Retrieve Ruto; the red barrier is gone. The timed bubble room gives the optional Compass. Defeat the blue tentacle in the right branch, then the green tentacle in the central branch, using the Boomerang on jellyfish too.`),e(`bigocto`,`Recover the Spiritual Stone`,`Carry Ruto back into the floor-hole room. Drop through the hole previously blocked by the green tentacle, near the right side when entering from the branching corridor. Throw Ruto onto the raised stone platform. Bigocto appears: stun it with the Boomerang, get behind it, stun the exposed rear and strike with the sword. Repeat, then ride the central platform upward.`),e(`moving-platforms`,`Cross the trembling platforms`,`Stun each red moving platform with the Boomerang before using it. Continue until a new platform lowers you into the earlier elevator room. Put a wooden crate on the blue floor switch and enter the final passage.`),e(`last-switch`,`Curve a throw around the barrier`,`Clear the jellyfish, climb the vines and aim the Boomerang around the transparent barrier at the ceiling switch. Move sideways to give the throw enough curve. Enter the boss room. After Barinade, collect the heart and use the blue light; Ruto gives Zora's Sapphire.`)],boss:{name:`Barinade`,strategy:[`Keep circling while targeting the three tentacles attached to the ceiling. Boomerang hits sever them.`,`Stun the body when exposed, then clear the rotating jellyfish with the Boomerang. In the final phase, stun the core again and slash it while it is vulnerable; move away when the electricity resumes.`]},notes:[`If Ruto disappears after a fall or leaving a room, revisit the room where you first carried her. Do not abandon the quest assuming she is permanently lost.`,`A bottle holding a fish cannot also hold a fairy. Empty it first when you need a different item.`],sources:[t(8,`Zora's River and Ruto's letter`),t(9,`Jabu-Jabu`),n(`jabu-jabus-belly`,`Dungeon route`),r(`inside-jabu-jabus-belly`,`Ruto and Barinade`)]},{slug:`door-of-time`,title:`The Door of Time`,subtitle:`Seven years between two breaths.`,description:`Open the Temple of Time, awaken as adult Link and recover the Hookshot from Dampe's grave.`,era:`Both ages`,region:`Hyrule Castle Town · Kakariko`,reward:`Master Sword · Light Medallion · Hookshot · Song of Storms`,prerequisites:[`All three Spiritual Stones`,`A bottle recommended`],steps:[e(`ocarina`,`Return to the castle drawbridge`,`Approach Castle Town from Hyrule Field. After the escape scene, dive into the moat and retrieve the Ocarina of Time. Zelda's message teaches the Song of Time.`),e(`door`,`Open the Door of Time`,`Enter the Temple of Time through the path beside the market. Stand before its altar and play the Song of Time. With all three Spiritual Stones collected, the door opens. Enter and pull the Master Sword.`),e(`adult`,`Listen to Rauru and Sheik`,`The story moves seven years ahead. Rauru gives you the Light Medallion; Sheik explains the temples. Leave through the ruined market and cross the field toward Kakariko Village.`),e(`grave`,`Enter Dampe's grave`,`Go to the graveyard. On the left, locate the grave marked by flowers where Dampe is buried. Pull it back and descend. Speak to his ghost and follow his race, avoiding the flames he drops and choosing quick turns at the forks.`),e(`hookshot`,`Take the Hookshot`,`Finish the race before the final door closes and speak to Dampe. Open the chest for the Hookshot. A time under one minute is not required for this item. Beyond the chest, play the Song of Time by the blue block to clear the exit and climb into the windmill.`),e(`storms`,`Remember the windmill's song`,`As adult Link, speak to the windmill musician and show him the Ocarina. Repeat the Song of Storms. This creates access to the Bottom of the Well when you revisit Kakariko as a child later.`),e(`meadow`,`Find the temple above the meadow`,`Return to Kokiri Forest. In the Lost Woods, take right, left, right; play Saria's Song to Mido so he lets you pass, then continue left, straight, left, right. Pass the Moblins in the meadow using corners and the Hookshot from safe angles. Dodge the club-wielding Moblin's shock waves, then climb to Sheik.`),e(`minuet`,`Learn the Minuet of Forest`,`After Sheik teaches the warp song, aim the Hookshot at the branch above the temple entrance. Pull yourself up and enter the Forest Temple.`)],notes:[`You cannot freely return to childhood until after the Forest Temple. Complete that temple, then meet Sheik again at the Temple of Time.`,`Epona is optional for this route: later, the Longshot can cross the broken Gerudo Valley bridge.`],sources:[t(10,`Temple of Time`),t(11,`Adult Kakariko and Lost Woods`),n(`forest-temple`,`Reaching the Forest Temple`)]},{slug:`forest-temple`,title:`Forest Temple`,subtitle:`Four flames lost in a haunted house.`,description:`Find the Fairy Bow, restore the Poe flames and defeat Phantom Ganon.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Sacred Forest Meadow`,reward:`Fairy Bow · Forest Medallion · travel between ages`,prerequisites:[`Hookshot`,`Song of Time`,`Minuet of Forest`],steps:[e(`entry-keys`,`Gather two opening keys`,`In the first courtyard, climb the vines on the right, cross the branches and Hookshot the chest for a Small Key. Enter the temple. After the four Poes remove the lobby flames, take the north door and defeat both Stalfos for another key.`),e(`well-key`,`Drain the courtyard well`,`In the lobby's northwest corner, remove the blue block with the Song of Time. Cross the courtyard and climb its vines, clearing Skullwalltulas first. Defeat the Blue Bubble for the map, then exit to the other courtyard. Hookshot to the switch ledge and step on it. The well drains: descend for the third key.`),e(`block-room`,`Build a path through the block room`,`Return to the lobby and unlock the west door. Beyond the Blue Bubble, follow the floor arrows to pull and push the large green block into its socket. Climb up and work around to move the red block into place. Use both as stairs to the upper locked door.`),e(`bow`,`Follow the twisted corridor`,`Unlock the upper door, cross the twisted passage and watch for the Wallmaster in the next chamber. Unlock the next door, descend the portrait stairway and enter the Stalfos arena. Defeat the first Stalfos; when two arrive on the lowered platform, finish both before either revives. Take the Fairy Bow.`),e(`first-poes`,`Restore the red and blue flames`,`In each portrait stairway on either side of the bow room, stand back and shoot the painting showing a Poe. Repeat until it leaves the last painting, then follow and fight it. Arrows work while it is visible. Collect the Small Key and Compass left by the two sisters.`),e(`untwist`,`Untwist the west passage`,`Return through the block room to the eye above the twisted corridor entrance. Shoot it to straighten the passage. Cross again: the ornate chest is now reachable and contains the Boss Key. Drop through the nearby floor opening, clear the Bubbles and exit onto an upper courtyard ledge.`),e(`floormaster`,`Win the courtyard key`,`Enter the small side room off that ledge and defeat its Floormaster, including all three smaller hands before they reunite. Take the Small Key. Return through the courtyard and block room; shoot the eye again to restore the twisted corridor.`),e(`frozen-eye`,`Twist the opposite wing`,`Cross the bow room and climb the blue-Poe stairs. Spend your keys on the upper route. In the room with rotating platforms, shoot an arrow through the central torch into the frozen eye. Return to the now-twisted passage and drop through the hole.`),e(`ceiling`,`Cross the falling ceiling`,`Watch one ceiling cycle before moving. Stand where its holes leave safe spaces, advance to the floor switch and then reach the opened door. Do not stop beneath a solid section of ceiling.`),e(`green-poe`,`Assemble the green portrait`,`Shoot the large painting to begin the timed block puzzle. Push the four picture blocks together into the completed Poe image; leave the plain blue block aside. Defeat the green sister after she appears. Continue back to the main lobby.`),e(`meg`,`Identify Meg`,`The final Poe splits into four copies. Watch the one that spins as they appear: that is the real Meg. Shoot her and repeat until the purple flame returns. The lobby elevator is now usable.`),e(`basement`,`Rotate the basement`,`Ride down. Push the handles on the central wall to turn the room, checking the newly exposed alcoves after each rotation. Press the three floor switches to remove the bars along the boss route. Use the Boss Key and enter the arena.`),e(`time-travel`,`Reopen the path to childhood`,`Collect the heart and Forest Medallion after the fight. Return to the Temple of Time. Sheik teaches the Prelude of Light and explains that placing the Master Sword back in its pedestal returns Link to childhood. Pulling it again restores adulthood.`)],boss:{name:`Phantom Ganon`,strategy:[`During the painting phase, watch the riders: shoot the one emerging through purple energy; the decoy retreats.`,`In the second phase, bat the energy sphere back with the sword until it hits him. Run in and strike while he is down. Avoid his charge rather than trying to volley it.`]},notes:[`This is the original dungeon layout, not Master Quest. A twisted passage changes where its openings and chests sit.`,`The two Stalfos guarding the bow can revive if the other survives too long. Keep both fights under control before finishing them.`],sources:[n(`forest-temple`,`Temple puzzles`),t(12,`Forest Temple`),r(`forest-temple`,`Keys, Poes and Phantom Ganon`)]},{slug:`fire-temple`,title:`Fire Temple`,subtitle:`Leave no Goron behind.`,description:`Rescue the imprisoned Gorons, find the Megaton Hammer and bring down Volvagia.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Goron City · Death Mountain Crater`,reward:`Goron Tunic · Megaton Hammer · Fire Medallion`,prerequisites:[`Forest Temple complete`,`Bow`,`Bombs`,`Hookshot`],steps:[e(`tunic`,`Speak to the young Goron`,`In adult Goron City, stop the rolling Goron with a bomb. Speak to him about the dragon and the Gorons until he gives you the Goron Tunic. Equip it. Pull the statue in Darunia's room to reveal the crater passage; Hookshot across the broken bridge, learn the Bolero of Fire from Sheik and descend into the temple.`),e(`first-key`,`Meet Darunia and free a prisoner`,`In the lobby, climb the stairs and enter the left door. After speaking to Darunia, use the platforms on the left to reach a cell switch. Free the Goron and open his chest for a Small Key. Return to the lobby and unlock the right door.`),e(`lava-keys`,`Search both ends of the lava chamber`,`From the bridge, explore the left-side door for a second prisoner and key. On the opposite side, bomb the cracked wall to find another cell and key. Return to the bridge and unlock the far door.`),e(`geyser`,`Ride the fire lift`,`Slide down, climb the chain mesh and jump to the block above the fire geyser. Push the block onto it, stand on it and ride upward. Unlock the next door. In the Torch Slug room, move the block to climb to the upper ledge, then use a bomb on the crystal switch below to lower the flames while you climb the fence.`),e(`boulder-maze`,`Rescue both Gorons in the maze`,`On the lower floor of the rolling-boulder maze, work around the perimeter. One cell is opened by a nearby floor switch; another is through a side doorway. Rescue both and take both keys before using the locked exit.`),e(`upper-maze`,`Return above the rolling boulders`,`Cross the narrow upper passage; an eye switch opens the optional map room. Unlock the route into the rising-fire chamber, run up its grating and take the upper door back into the boulder maze. Bomb the cracked floor on the first raised platform. Climb down to a prisoner and key, then climb back up.`),e(`high-switch`,`Open the distant cell`,`Jump across the raised maze platforms to the floor switch. It opens the cell at the opposite end of this upper route. Reach it for another key. Return to the rising-fire chamber and take its other locked exit.`),e(`fire-maze`,`Work around the invisible fire walls`,`Navigate the large fire maze carefully; flames reveal themselves when you approach. Take the locked passage across the middle, passing a caged Goron you cannot yet free. On the far half, step on the timed switch and run to the temporarily lowered barrier. Bomb the fake door behind it to reveal the real entrance.`),e(`dancer`,`Defeat the first Flare Dancer`,`Target the dancer and Hookshot its small core out of the fire, then strike it while it flees. Repeat until it is defeated. Ride the central platform upward. In the next room, activate the crystal switch with a delayed bomb so you can climb the fence while its flames are down.`),e(`hammer`,`Race to the Megaton Hammer`,`At the top, step on the floor switch. Run along the narrow curved staircase before the chest's flames return. Open the chest for the Megaton Hammer; fall safely back and retry the switch if the timer expires.`),e(`hammer-path`,`Drive the platforms downward`,`Hammer the face block near the room entrance. Drop with it, smash the totem aside, then hammer the next floor section into a staircase. Carry a crate onto the blue switch below to keep its door open. Continue hammering the marked blocks and rusty switches.`),e(`last-small-key`,`Free the Goron below`,`At the Time Block, play the Song of Time to move it, cross and hammer the rusty switch. Drop to the cell it opens and collect its key. Return above and hammer the large column so it falls into the lava room where Darunia entered the boss door.`),e(`boss-key`,`Return to the lobby's ground floor`,`Go back to the entrance lobby. Hammer the totem blocking the ground-floor locked door. Clear the enemy rooms, defend against the flying tiles and defeat the second Flare Dancer. Hammer the rusty switch to free the final prisoner and collect the Boss Key.`),e(`volvagia`,`Cross to Volvagia`,`Return to Darunia's lava room by the lobby's upstairs left door. The lowered column now provides a route to the boss door. Win the battle, take the heart and enter the warp for the Fire Medallion.`)],boss:{name:`Volvagia`,strategy:[`When the dragon's head emerges, avoid its hair swipe, hammer the head and strike while it is stunned.`,`During flight, keep moving away from its fire breath. When it circles overhead, watch for falling rocks and their shadows. Save your close attacks for the next exposed head.`]},notes:[`Every rescued Goron's chest matters to this route. If a locked door stops you, check the cells on both levels of the rolling-boulder maze.`,`The Goron Tunic removes the heat countdown; it does not make lava or fire harmless.`],sources:[t(14,`Goron City and the crater`),t(15,`Fire Temple`),n(`fire-temple`,`Prisoners and hammer`),r(`fire-temple`,`Fire Temple route`)]},{slug:`ice-cavern`,title:`Ice Cavern`,subtitle:`A blue flame remembers the water.`,description:`Collect blue fire, solve the sliding-block room and recover the Iron Boots before the Water Temple.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Zora's Fountain`,reward:`Iron Boots · Serenade of Water · Zora Tunic`,prerequisites:[`At least one empty bottle`,`Hookshot`,`Zelda's Lullaby`],steps:[e(`icebergs`,`Reach the frozen fountain`,`Travel up Zora's River and play Zelda's Lullaby at the waterfall. In the frozen domain, go behind King Zora into the fountain. Jump across the ice floes toward the Ice Cavern entrance at the side of the lake.`),e(`first-rupees`,`Open the first silver-rupee door`,`Clear the Freezards in the entrance chamber. In the room with a rotating ice blade, collect all five silver rupees, including the raised one reached from the ledge. Avoid the falling icicles and continue through the opened passage.`),e(`blue-fire`,`Bottle blue fire`,`In the next chamber, fill an empty bottle from the blue flame. Release it against red ice to melt it; ordinary fire will not substitute. The map chest is beneath red ice here. Refill the bottle before returning to the rotating-blade chamber.`),e(`branch`,`Open the route to the block puzzle`,`Melt the red ice across the other blocked passages. One side branch contains the optional Compass and a Piece of Heart. The required branch reaches a room with a large sliding block, silver rupees and another blue flame.`),e(`block-rupees`,`Slide the block between the ledges`,`Kill the Ice Keese before starting. Push the block against the fixed ice pillars, climb it and jump to each silver-rupee ledge. A push continues until an obstacle stops the block. If it becomes unusable, push it into the abyss: a fresh block appears at its starting position.`),e(`ice-rupee`,`Melt the last silver rupee`,`Use the block to reach the blue-fire ledge and refill your bottle. Bring blue fire to the rupee sealed in red ice, in the alcove to the entrance's right. After collecting all five rupees, reset the block by pushing it off the edge. For the exit, keep directions relative to looking into the room from its entrance: push the new block left, away from the entrance toward the blue flame, right, back toward the entrance, then right again beneath the exit. Climb it and leave through the raised passage.`),e(`boots`,`Defeat the White Wolfos`,`Melt the final red ice in the passage. In the last chamber, guard against the White Wolfos and counterattack after its swipes. Open the chest for the Iron Boots. Sheik teaches the Serenade of Water.`),e(`thaw-king`,`Thaw King Zora`,`Equip the boots to sink through the pool behind the chest and use the underwater exit. Before leaving the cavern, refill at least one bottle with blue fire. Release it at King Zora's red ice and speak to him for the Zora Tunic.`)],notes:[`Keep one bottle free for blue fire. More bottles reduce trips, but one is enough.`,`The boots sink Link; the Zora Tunic removes the underwater breathing timer. These are separate pieces of equipment.`,`The sliding-block room is resettable. A mistaken push never permanently locks the dungeon.`],sources:[n(`ice-cavern`,`Ice Cavern`),t(16,`Blue fire and Iron Boots`),r(`ice-cavern`,`Sliding-block chamber`)]},{slug:`water-temple`,title:`Water Temple`,subtitle:`Read the water. Remember the room.`,description:`Follow the original N64 water-level sequence, collect all six Small Keys and recover the Longshot.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Lake Hylia`,reward:`Longshot · Water Medallion · Fire Arrows`,prerequisites:[`Iron Boots`,`Zora Tunic`,`Hookshot`,`Bow`,`Bombs`,`Song of Time`,`Zelda's Lullaby`],steps:[e(`entry`,`Enter beneath Lake Hylia`,`Wear the Zora Tunic and Iron Boots. Sink to the temple entrance in the lake and Hookshot its blue crystal to lift the gate. In the central room, sink to the bottom and take the passage between two torches to meet Ruto. Remove the boots and follow her upward.`),e(`low`,`Lower the water; collect key one`,`At the top of Ruto's shaft, play Zelda's Lullaby at the Triforce to lower the water fully. Drop back down. Use a lit arrow through the central torch, or Din's Fire, to light both doorway torches. Defeat the Shell Blades beyond for a Small Key: strike their exposed flesh when they open.`),e(`dragon-key`,`Find key two in the dragon room`,`Take the bottom west passage from the central room. Push its block until it falls, then follow the water route. Activate the crystal to raise a water spout and cross. In the swirling-water room, activate the crystal in the dragon's mouth, then quickly Hookshot the target beside the underwater gate. Pass through before it closes and surface to the key chest.`),e(`middle`,`Raise the water halfway`,`Return to the central room and spend a key on the central tower's ground-floor door. Hookshot upward to its inner ledge. Play Zelda's Lullaby at the Triforce to raise the water to the middle level.`),e(`hidden-floor`,`Look beneath the floating platform`,`Stay inside the tower. Sink into the opening exposed beneath the platform that floated upward. Activate the crystal below and defeat the released enemies. Swim through the ceiling opening they reveal for key three. Return to the main chamber.`),e(`bomb-key`,`Return to Ruto's shaft`,`Enter Ruto's bottom-floor passage again, then float only to the current middle waterline. Bomb the cracked wall there and take key four. Return to the main chamber.`),e(`high`,`Reach the highest water switch`,`Unlock the west door on the middle level. Stand on the water spout and activate its crystal so it carries you up. Follow the passage to the high Triforce and raise the water fully. Before leaving this level, enter the east passage and pull its block as far as it will go; you need that access later.`),e(`waterfall`,`Climb the falling platforms`,`Unlock the top-floor west door. Descend to the lowest platform and use the Hookshot targets on the moving platforms to climb the waterfall. Unlock the door at the top.`),e(`dragon-heads`,`Raise and lower the dragon statues`,`Shoot the crystal to raise the heads, then Hookshot the first. Lower them, Hookshot the wall target across the room and climb over the lowered head. Raise them again to reach the next head. Lower once more, stand on that head and raise it beneath your feet to reach the exit. Clear the enemies and cross to the next room.`),e(`dark-link`,`Face Dark Link`,`Walk to the far side of the shallow lake, then return toward the central tree to make your double appear. Use unpredictable close attacks; the Megaton Hammer or Din's Fire can bypass his sword counters. Defeat him and take the Longshot from the following chest.`),e(`river-key`,`Find key five beyond the river`,`Play the Song of Time behind the Longshot chest to remove the floor block. Follow the river carefully around its vortices. Near the end, shoot the eye and Longshot to the chest through the briefly opened grate. Take the key, then return through the dragon-water route to the main room.`),e(`block-key`,`Collect key six at middle water`,`Lower the water using Ruto's upper Triforce, then raise it halfway inside the central tower. On the middle south side, shoot the eye and Longshot across the timed gate. Follow the passage to the block you prepared earlier. Move it to reach the last Small Key.`),e(`north-route`,`Use the bottom north passage`,`Sink to the bottom north passage. Longshot across the spikes and unlock the door. Cross the room with water currents and rolling boulders to its opposite door; the Iron Boots help you hold your position when appropriate.`),e(`stone-switch`,`Hold down the submerged switch`,`In the Stinger room, bomb the two weak wall sections to access both sides of the block. Push and pull it around the opened passage until it drops onto the floor switch. The water rises, allowing you to reach the next door.`),e(`boss-key`,`Reach the Boss Key`,`Step on the next switch and cross the three raised water spouts before they fall. Beyond, avoid the rolling boulder and follow the submerged passage, defeating the Shell Blade. Surface, spend your remaining key and open the ornate Boss Key chest.`),e(`boss-door`,`Restore the high water`,`Return to the central room. Use the middle west spout route to reach the top Triforce again and raise the water fully. Longshot to the dragon target on the north side, then run up the slippery slope while avoiding its moving blade traps. Enter the boss door.`),e(`fire-arrows`,`Shoot into the sunrise`,`After Morpha, take the heart and the blue warp for the Water Medallion. Lake Hylia refills. On the lakeside platform with the inscription, face the rising sun and shoot a normal arrow into it. Swim to the little island where the Fire Arrows land and collect them for Ganon's Castle.`)],boss:{name:`Morpha`,strategy:[`Target the small nucleus inside the water tentacle. Pull it onto land with the Longshot, then strike it with the sword.`,`Stay near a corner with room to retreat. Move away when a tentacle reaches toward you: a successful grab throws Link hard. Repeat the pull-and-strike cycle.`]},notes:[`Six Small Keys are used in this original-quest route. The most commonly missed one is beneath the floating platform inside the central tower.`,`N64 Iron Boots are equipped from the pause equipment screen. The 3DS touch-screen shortcut is not part of the original controls.`,`Low, middle and high water are controlled at three different Triforce marks; play Zelda’s Lullaby at the corresponding mark to change the water level.`],sources:[n(`water-temple`,`Water levels and keys`),t(17,`Water Temple`),r(`water-temple`,`Original Water Temple route`)]},{slug:`bottom-of-the-well`,title:`Bottom of the Well`,subtitle:`Believe what the eye cannot see.`,description:`Return to childhood, drain Kakariko's well and retrieve the Lens of Truth without unnecessary key detours.`,era:`Both ages`,region:`Kakariko Village`,reward:`Nocturne of Shadow · Lens of Truth`,prerequisites:[`Forest, Fire and Water Medallions`,`Song of Storms`,`Access to childhood`,`Magic meter`],steps:[e(`nocturne`,`Witness Kakariko's shadow`,`Visit Kakariko as an adult after completing the Forest, Fire and Water Temples. Watch the scene in the village and learn the Nocturne of Shadow from Sheik. If you have not learned the Song of Storms, visit the windmill musician now and show him the Ocarina.`),e(`child`,`Return as a child`,`Travel to the Temple of Time and place the Master Sword in its pedestal. Return to Kakariko's windmill as child Link and play the Song of Storms for the musician. The mechanism speeds up and drains the well outside.`),e(`false-wall`,`Enter the hidden chamber`,`Climb down the dry well and crawl through the narrow opening. Descend the ladder, defeat the Skulltula and walk through the apparently solid wall behind it. The dungeon uses false walls and floors, so move deliberately.`),e(`drain`,`Drain the inner channels`,`Follow the shallow channel around the outer edge of the main chamber, avoiding the suspicious center. At the far end, find the large stone face pouring water and play Zelda's Lullaby on its Triforce mark. The channels drain.`),e(`crawl`,`Follow the newly exposed tunnel`,`Return toward the entrance of the main chamber. Drop into the drained pit just inside the false wall and crawl through its small tunnel. Defeat the Skulltula, climb the vines or ladder and enter Dead Hand's room.`),e(`dead-hand`,`Defeat Dead Hand`,`Allow a floor hand to grab Link so the main creature emerges. Move the control stick and press buttons to break free. When Dead Hand lowers its head toward you, strike its head with the sword, then retreat from its bite. Repeat the sequence until the chest appears.`),e(`lens`,`Take the Lens of Truth`,`Open the large chest for the Lens of Truth. Equip and activate it to distinguish real openings from illusions. Its use consumes magic, so switch it off when the room is understood.`),e(`return-adult`,`Prepare for the Shadow Temple`,`Retrace the crawlspace and entrance ladder to leave. Return to the Temple of Time and become adult Link. Refill magic, bring Din's Fire and play the Nocturne of Shadow to reach the high graveyard entrance.`)],notes:[`This main-story route goes directly to the Lens. The well's other chests, three Small Keys and Gold Skulltulas are optional for reaching that item.`,`The Lens reveals a route; it does not create a floor where none exists. Keep watching Link's actual footing.`],sources:[n(`under-the-well`,`Direct Lens route`),t(13,`The well`),t(18,`Nocturne and Shadow Temple`)]},{slug:`shadow-temple`,title:`Shadow Temple`,subtitle:`A whisper beneath every stone.`,description:`Cross the invisible paths, sail the funeral boat and confront Bongo Bongo.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Kakariko Graveyard`,reward:`Hover Boots · Shadow Medallion`,prerequisites:[`Nocturne of Shadow`,`Lens of Truth`,`Din's Fire and magic`,`Longshot`,`Bow`,`Bombs`,`Iron Boots`],steps:[e(`torches`,`Open the entrance`,`Warp with the Nocturne of Shadow. In the circular entrance chamber, stand on the central platform and cast Din's Fire to light all the torches together. Enter, Longshot across the first gap and pass through the false wall.`),e(`boots`,`Find the Hover Boots first`,`Use the Lens around the bird statue to identify the true skull marker; turn the statue's beak toward it to open the far gate. Before crossing, explore the false wall on the right and the rooms beyond. Use the Lens to follow hidden doors to Dead Hand. Defeat it by escaping a hand's grip and striking its lowered head; take the Hover Boots.`),e(`hub`,`Cross the first abyss`,`Wear the Hover Boots and run straight across the short gap to the opened gate. In the Beamos hub, explore the side passage with two spinning blades. Collect all five silver rupees to open the room containing the first Small Key. Bomb the cracked wall in the hub and unlock the main route.`),e(`guillotines`,`Pass the guillotine hall`,`Advance one blade at a time and watch for a falling Wallmaster. Cross the platform with the Stalfos. Use the moving platforms on the right to reach the silver-rupee chamber. One rupee is under the Beamos; bomb it. Collect the set to open the next room.`),e(`crushers`,`Support the falling spikes`,`Use the Lens to reveal a block in the wall at the right of the crushing-spike room. Pull it beneath the crushers so you can pass safely. Climb onto the upper structure, press its floor switch and reach the chest it reveals for key two.`),e(`hidden-platforms`,`Cross the invisible ledges`,`Return to the large guillotine chamber. Use the Lens to find the platforms leading past the final blade to a locked door. Inside, reveal the hidden floor spikes and collect all silver rupees, using the ceiling Longshot targets for the raised ones.`),e(`skull-key`,`Bomb the giant skull`,`The rupee door leads to a room with a rotating skull. Kill all the Keese so you can leave, climb up and drop a Bomb Flower into the skull's opening. Collect key three from the debris. Return and use the invisible Longshot target above the locked door.`),e(`fans`,`Use both kinds of boots`,`Wear the Iron Boots to walk against the fans. Longshot to the wooden beam above the gap when needed. At the far end, reveal the false side wall with the Lens. Switch to the Hover Boots and let the fan carry you through that opening.`),e(`fourth-key`,`Search the small mound`,`In the next enemy room, bomb the mound just to the right of where you entered. Use the Lens to reveal the chest containing key four. Defeat the Gibdos if the exit is barred, then open the locked door.`),e(`boat`,`Sail the ancient boat`,`Move the block beneath the ladder and climb aboard. Play Zelda's Lullaby on the Triforce. Fight the Stalfos while the boat moves. As it reaches the end and starts sinking, jump to the bank on the left.`),e(`maze`,`Collect both final keys`,`Go through the bank's side door into the invisible-wall maze. Use the Lens to navigate. In the room with two approaching wooden spike walls, cast Din's Fire to burn them and take the Boss Key. In the invisible Floormaster room, defeat the large hand and all its little hands for the final Small Key.`),e(`bridge`,`Topple the statue`,`Return to the bank where you left the boat. Shoot the Bomb Flowers across the abyss; the explosion drops the statue into a bridge. Cross, unlock the far door and follow the Lens-revealed platforms with the Hover Boots to the boss entrance.`),e(`medallion`,`Awaken the Shadow Sage`,`Defeat Bongo Bongo, collect the Heart Container and use the blue warp. With the Shadow Medallion earned, your next destination is the Gerudo fortress in western Hyrule.`)],boss:{name:`Bongo Bongo`,strategy:[`Shoot each hand with an arrow to stun both. Keep the Lens active when you need to see the eye and body.`,`Shoot the exposed eye as it approaches, then close in for sword attacks. Repeat after the hands recover. Hover Boots soften the disruption from the drum but make movement slippery.`]},notes:[`Switch the Lens off between invisible puzzles to conserve magic. Pots often contain refills.`,`The Hover Boots only suspend Link briefly; start close to a ledge and run decisively. They do not allow sustained flight.`],sources:[n(`shadow-temple`,`Temple route`),t(18,`Shadow Temple`),r(`shadow-temple`,`Invisible paths and Bongo Bongo`)]},{slug:`gerudo-and-wasteland`,title:`Gerudo & the wasteland`,subtitle:`Beyond the last flag, follow a ghost.`,description:`Free all four carpenters, earn the Gerudo card and cross the desert to learn the Requiem of Spirit.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Gerudo Valley · Haunted Wasteland`,reward:`Gerudo Membership Card · Requiem of Spirit`,prerequisites:[`Longshot or Epona for the broken bridge`,`Bow`,`Lens of Truth and magic`,`Hover Boots or Longshot for the sand river`],steps:[e(`valley`,`Cross the broken bridge`,`Enter Gerudo Valley from western Hyrule Field. Jump the broken bridge on Epona, or Longshot the wood on the far side. Speak to the carpenter boss by the tent, then follow the path into Gerudo's Fortress.`),e(`prison`,`Work from the fortress's lower entrance`,`Guards outside capture you if they spot you; arrows temporarily stun them. If captured, use the Longshot on the wood above the prison window to escape. Drop to the ground and take the nearby left doorway into the fortress.`),e(`first-carpenter`,`Free the first carpenter`,`Find the cell and talk to its captive. A Gerudo Thief drops in. Block normal blows and dodge her leaping attack, which can send you back to jail. Counterattack after she misses. Pick up her key, open the cell and speak to the carpenter so he actually leaves.`),e(`second-carpenter`,`Reach the upper cell`,`Leave by the doorway near the freed carpenter. Enter the next opening to the left, follow the interior past its patrolling guard and leave through the right-hand exit. Outside, follow the ledge left, stun the guard above and climb to the upper doorway. Defeat the second Thief and release the next carpenter.`),e(`third-carpenter`,`Drop to the lower passage`,`Take the exit on the right side of the second cell room. Climb down the vines and enter the doorway directly ahead for another prisoner. Talk to him, win the fight, open his cell and speak again.`),e(`fourth-carpenter`,`Find the final cell`,`Return up the vines and enter the left doorway. Stun the two guards in the lower area, cross it and climb the far ramp to the outside. From that exit, drop onto the lower ledge to the right and enter its door. Wait for the corridor guard, stun her, then follow the right-hand passage to the fourth carpenter.`),e(`membership`,`Take the membership card`,`After freeing and speaking to all four carpenters, accept the Gerudo Membership Card. Guards no longer arrest you for exploring the fortress. Go to the northwestern desert gate, climb its ladder and speak to the gatekeeper to open it.`),e(`flags`,`Follow the desert markers`,`Across the gate, traverse the sand river with the Hover Boots or Longshot to the crates on the other side. Follow the line of flags through the storm. Keep the last flag visible until you identify the next; walking into the unmarked desert returns you to the start.`),e(`poe`,`Follow the invisible guide`,`Reach the stone shelter and climb onto its roof. Activate the Lens to reveal a Poe guide. Follow its path through the storm, avoiding the Leevers and maintaining enough magic to see it. Near the far flags, continue toward the Desert Colossus as the guide turns back.`),e(`requiem`,`Learn the route across time`,`Enter the Spirit Temple and inspect its entrance: the crawlspace is too small for adult Link and the great block is too heavy. Leave. Sheik appears and teaches the Requiem of Spirit. Warp to the Temple of Time, return to childhood and use the Requiem to reach the Colossus as a child.`)],notes:[`You need all four rescue conversations, not only four defeated guards, to earn the card.`,`The Gerudo Training Ground and its Ice Arrows are optional. They are not required for the Spirit Temple or the final battle.`],sources:[n(`carpenter-rescue`,`Four carpenters`),t(19,`Gerudo Fortress`),n(`journey-desert-colossus`,`Wasteland crossing`),t(20,`Desert Colossus`)]},{slug:`spirit-temple`,title:`Spirit Temple`,subtitle:`Two ages. One promise to keep.`,description:`Complete the child and adult halves of the Spirit Temple, recover the Mirror Shield and face Twinrova.`,era:`Both ages`,region:`Desert Colossus`,reward:`Silver Gauntlets · Mirror Shield · Spirit Medallion`,prerequisites:[`Requiem of Spirit`,`Child and adult access`,`Boomerang`,`Bombs`,`Din's Fire`,`Longshot`,`Bow`,`Lens`,`Hammer`,`Hover Boots`],steps:[e(`nabooru`,`Child: make a promise to Nabooru`,`Enter as child Link. Speak to Nabooru by the left crawlspace, say you dislike Ganondorf and agree to help. Crawl through, defeat the Keese and Armos, then take the left door.`),e(`child-loop`,`Child: lower the metal bridge`,`Defeat the Stalfos and the Green Bubble when its flame is down. Throw the Boomerang around the metal barrier to strike the crystal behind it. Cross the lowered bridge. In the next room, defeat the Anubis with Din's Fire, or activate the flame switch and guide its mirrored movement into the fire.`),e(`child-key`,`Child: earn the first key`,`Collect the five silver rupees in the next room, watching for a Wallmaster overhead. Cross the lowered barrier and light the two unlit torches with a burning Deku Stick. Take the key and exit back to the first chamber. Crawl through its central passage and unlock the door.`),e(`sunlight`,`Child: let the sunlight in`,`Shoot the spiders on the climbable wall and climb. Defeat the Lizalfos. Hit the crystal switch to get Bombchus, then send one up the wall toward the cracked patch where sunlight leaks in. Its explosion widens the opening and activates the sun emblem.`),e(`statue`,`Child: cross the statue chamber`,`In the giant-statue room, push the nearby Armos off the ledge onto its floor switch. Climb the stairs and continue. Lighting the two torches on the room's lower floor earns the optional map; the climbable wall beside the dropped Armos returns you upstairs.`),e(`sun-block`,`Child: move the sun into the light`,`In the block chamber, collect five silver rupees to light a torch. Use it to light the other three torches and take the Small Key. Move the plain blocks aside, then push the sun-marked block into the shaft of light. Follow the opened route and unlock the Iron Knuckle room.`),e(`silver`,`Child: collect the Silver Gauntlets`,`Wake the Iron Knuckle. Bait an axe swing, backflip clear and punish its recovery with the sword; pillars it breaks can release hearts. After winning, leave through the rear door and open the outdoor chest. Watch Nabooru's scene. Return to the Temple of Time, become adult Link and warp back.`),e(`adult-block`,`Adult: open the other wing`,`Push the giant block on the entrance's right side until it drops. Bomb the Beamos and Longshot the ceiling crystal. The left room offers a Compass after a Wolfos fight and Zelda's Lullaby. Take the right door for the required silver-rupee room.`),e(`adult-key`,`Adult: collect the boulder-room rupees`,`Use the Hover Boots for the floating rupee and check the alcoves. Move the Time Block with the Song of Time to reach the remaining rupee. Collect all five, enter the opened door, defeat the Like Like and take its key. Return and unlock the central route.`),e(`mirror-room`,`Adult: direct the light`,`Pass the flying pots and Like Like, then climb the brick wall. Use the Lens to locate the invisible Floormaster; defeat it and its small hands. Rotate the mirror until its light strikes the sun that opens the exit. Avoid continuing to the sun that releases a Wallmaster.`),e(`hand-key`,`Adult: play in the statue's hand`,`Back in the giant-statue chamber, climb the stairs and Hover onto the hand marked with a Triforce. Play Zelda's Lullaby. Longshot to the chest that falls onto the other hand and take its Small Key. Return using the ceiling target above the Armos.`),e(`anubis`,`Adult: clear the fire puzzle`,`Climb the eastern stairs and unlock the door. Defeat the Beamos and the three Anubis beyond; Din's Fire is straightforward, or use the fire switch and their mirrored movement. In the next room, wake an Armos so it hops onto the blue switch, then run through the south door before it moves away.`),e(`mirror-shield`,`Adult: win the Mirror Shield`,`Climb the stairs to a second Iron Knuckle. Fight it using the same bait-and-counter rhythm, then open the chest outside for the Mirror Shield. Return to the Armos-switch room, stand in the sunlight and angle the shield onto the wall's sun. Take the key behind the opened door.`),e(`boss-key`,`Adult: secure the Boss Key`,`Return through the Anubis room and open its remaining locked door. Longshot high onto the moving climbing wall to pass it. Continue to the Triforce and play Zelda's Lullaby. In the next room, smash or bomb the false door hiding an eye switch, shoot the eye, Longshot to the new platform and step on its switch. Open the Boss Key chest.`),e(`mirrors`,`Adult: carry light to the giant face`,`Back outside the key room, take the upper passage. Strike the crystal through the bars with a sword spin to open the route. Defeat the Lizalfos and White Bubbles, bomb the cracked wall and rotate both mirrors so the light passes through the opening and bars into the room with the chained platform.`),e(`face`,`Adult: lower the platform`,`Stand on the chained platform and use the Mirror Shield to illuminate the sun switch. As the platform lowers into the statue chamber, hold the beam on the giant statue's face until it crumbles. Longshot to the opening, use the Boss Key and defeat the final Iron Knuckle. Continue through the passage to Twinrova.`),e(`spirit`,`Receive the Spirit Medallion`,`Win both phases of Twinrova, take the Heart Container and enter the warp. With all five temple sages awakened, return to the Temple of Time for the final revelation and the Light Arrows.`)],boss:{name:`Twinrova`,strategy:[`First, reflect one witch's elemental beam into the other with the Mirror Shield: ice into the fire witch, fire into the ice witch. Aim without targeting if you need freer shield control.`,`After they merge, absorb three attacks of the same element. Dodge the opposite element so it does not cancel the charge. Aim the released beam at Twinrova, jump across while she is stunned and attack with the sword. Return to the central platform and repeat.`]},notes:[`The Silver Gauntlets cannot be used by child Link. Their purpose is to open the adult entrance after the outdoor scene.`,`The original N64 barred crystal in the mirror section is reached with a sword spin; do not follow instructions for the relocated 3DS switch.`,`Ice Arrows are unnecessary. Fire for Anubis, reflected sunlight and the Mirror Shield solve the required puzzles.`],sources:[n(`spirit-temple-young`,`Child half`),t(21,`Child Spirit Temple`),n(`spirit-temple-adult`,`Adult half and Twinrova`),t(23,`Adult Spirit Temple`),r(`spirit-temple`,`Spirit Temple`)]},{slug:`ganons-castle`,title:`Ganon's Castle`,subtitle:`The courage to finish what began in a forest.`,description:`Break the six barriers, climb the tower and complete the original Ocarina of Time story.`,era:`Adult Link`,region:`Ganon's Castle`,reward:`Golden Gauntlets · Hyrule's future`,prerequisites:[`All six Medallions`,`Light Arrows from the Temple of Time`,`Fire Arrows`,`Mirror Shield`,`Lens and magic`,`All dungeon equipment`,`An empty bottle`],steps:[e(`bridge`,`Cross the sages' bridge`,`Visit the Temple of Time after all five adult temples to receive the Light Arrows. Refill arrows, magic and bottles, then go where Hyrule Castle stood. Approach the broken staircase at the chasm: the sages create a rainbow bridge. Enter and pass the Beamos to the barrier chamber.`),e(`shadow-gauntlets`,`Shadow trial: obtain the Golden Gauntlets`,`Take the purple-marked door first. Longshot to the chest, then light the torch with a Fire Arrow to reveal temporary platforms. Cross with the Hover Boots. Use the Lens for the hidden path, reach the lower floor switch and press it. Longshot to the large chest it creates and take the Golden Gauntlets.`),e(`shadow-clear`,`Shadow trial: destroy the orb`,`Follow the other invisible path to the rusty switch and hammer it. Reach the opened door using the Lens. Shoot the barrier orb with a Light Arrow. Every trial ends this way; ordinary arrows cannot destroy an orb.`),e(`forest`,`Forest trial: master the fans`,`Defeat the Wolfos. Light the lower torches with Din's Fire and the high torch with a Fire Arrow. In the fan room, gather all five silver rupees with the Hover Boots; use Iron Boots when you need to resist the wind. Bomb the Beamos and press the floor switch to raise the Longshot target beneath the high rupee. Enter and destroy the green orb.`),e(`water`,`Water trial: solve the ice blocks`,`Defeat the Freezards, bottle blue fire, melt the red ice and refill before leaving. In the timed block room, push the far block into the hole. Use it as a stopper for the remaining block: slide that block toward the filled hole, then toward the back and across beneath the high red-ice ledge. Climb, melt the ice, hammer the switch and destroy the blue orb.`),e(`fire`,`Fire trial: lift the great pillar`,`Equip the Goron Tunic. Collect five silver rupees across the lava platforms; keep moving on sinking sections. The Golden Gauntlets let you lift the huge pillar, exposing one rupee and creating access toward another. Use the Longshot target near the exit after collecting all five, then destroy the red orb.`),e(`light`,`Light trial: distrust the empty room`,`Lift the huge pillar blocking the yellow-marked door. Use the Lens to find and defeat invisible Keese and a Skulltula; take the key from the revealed chest. Unlock the route, play Zelda's Lullaby on the Triforce for another key, then collect the five silver rupees in the boulder room, including the one under the ceiling target. Beyond, run through the false back wall and destroy the real yellow orb.`),e(`spirit`,`Spirit trial: use light and a Bombchu`,`Bomb the Beamos and move the statues to collect the silver rupees around the blade traps. In the next room, strike the close crystal for Bombchus. Send one up the fence and through the gap to the farther switch. In the sun room, shoot a Fire Arrow at the web overhead, then reflect sunlight onto the correct sun beside the passage you entered through. Avoid the Wallmaster and destroy the orange orb.`),e(`refill`,`Prepare for the tower`,`With all six barriers gone, refill before entering the central tower. A Lens-revealed opening on the lower outer wall hides fairies and merchants. You may also leave the castle, lift the giant pillar outside and visit the Great Fairy for enhanced defense; this upgrade is helpful but optional.`),e(`tower`,`Climb through the final guards`,`Defeat the Dinolfos, then the Stalfos on the next combat floor and take the Boss Key. Continue to the two Iron Knuckles; wake one at a time if possible. Unlock the boss door and climb the last staircase. Leave the pots below intact for emergency supplies.`),e(`ganondorf`,`Break Ganondorf's defenses`,`Stay near the arena's outside edge. Return his energy ball with sword swings until it hits him, then immediately shoot a Light Arrow. Cross to his platform and strike while he is stunned; retreat before he recovers. For the clustered magic attack, dodge or return it with a timed spin. If you fall, refill from the pots and climb back using the central pillar.`),e(`escape`,`Follow Zelda out of the tower`,`After the fight, follow Zelda through the collapsing tower before the timer runs out. Stop at gates so she can open them. When fire traps her, defeat both Stalfos quickly. Continue outside, then approach the rubble to trigger the last battle.`),e(`sword`,`Recover the Master Sword`,`Ganon knocks the Master Sword beyond the fire. Use the Megaton Hammer, or Biggoron's Sword if you earned it, against his tail. A Light Arrow to his face creates an opening; move behind him and attack. When he collapses and the flames fall, retrieve and equip the Master Sword.`),e(`ending`,`Finish the battle`,`Continue reaching his tail after stunning or evading him. Keep enough magic for useful Light Arrows; rolling beneath him is another way around when the opening is clear. When Zelda restrains him, approach and use the Master Sword for the final blow. Let the ending play.`)],boss:{name:`Ganondorf → Ganon`,strategy:[`Ganondorf requires two linked openings: win the energy volley, then land a Light Arrow before moving in with the sword.`,`Ganon's tail is vulnerable. During the first phase the Hammer substitutes for your missing sword; retrieve the Master Sword as soon as Zelda calls you, and use it for the finishing strike.`]},notes:[`The Golden Gauntlets from the Shadow trial are required in the Fire and Light routes, so collect them first.`,`Keep your Hylian Shield available if buying from the hidden Deku merchants: the Mirror Shield does not reflect their nuts.`,`This completes the main story. Optional collectibles and side quests remain separate from this walkthrough's completion meter.`],sources:[n(`ganons-castle`,`Six trials`),t(24,`Ganondorf's Castle`),t(25,`Tower and ending`),r(`ganons-castle`,`Final dungeon`),n(`final-dungeon-preparations`,`Final preparations`)]}];a.map(e=>e.slug);var o=e=>a.find(t=>t.slug===e);export{i as n,o as r,a as t};